From 1ed951f1a57ec70addfbee458145368448d0ce8e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 4 Jul 2026 16:25:15 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat: opt-in conditional auto-merge rules engine

Add a pure, unit-testable merge-rules evaluator plus a thin, opt-in
'forge merge --auto <pr>' command. The evaluator ANDs composable,
config-driven rules over an already-fetched PR context (no network);
the command reads merge.auto from .forge/config.yaml and merges only
when enabled AND all rules pass. Absent/disabled config is a strict
no-op, preserving the never-auto-merge-by-default invariant.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
